ose together what  did they end up hitting each other  you'll be surprised to learn that this  picture is totally real and it belongs  to the Blue Angels the US Navy's flight  demonstration squadron although any  other planes that fly this close  together might crash this is completely  normal for the Blue Angels their history  dates back to when the team was first  formed in 1949 since then they started  gaining a reputation for their  spectacular aerobatic maneuvers there  are 11 Jets currently in the squadron  and through the  years there have been two hundred and  sixty one demonstration pilots in total  blue angels jets can travel the speed of  up to 700 miles per hour and during  their shows you will see them perform  their aerobatics sometimes just 18  inches apart their shows are always  incredible and this picture alone can  prove that in fact 11 million spectators  see their shows every year with an  additional 50,000 from March through  November the purpose of their shows is  to showcase the pride and  professionalism of the United States  Navy and Marine Corp they want to  inspire a culture of excellence and  service to country through flight  demonstration and community outreach and  it's certainly working a hole in the sky  there's probably a better way to  describe this fascinating photo than  saying there's a cloud hole in the sky  with a rainbow you might even think that  it belongs to a UFO sighting luckily  there's a way better explanation to this  phenomenon this formation is completely  natural and definitely not photoshopped  this particular photograph was taken in  eastern Victoria in Australia so here's  how sky holes like this one happen the  water temperature and the clouds has to  reach a freezing point but is not yet  frozen due to the lack of ice nucleation  what actually creates this hole is  called the Bergeron process which causes  the water droplets around a large number  of ice crystals to evaporate these ice  crystals often form when a plane passes  through the cloud and cools the air  the rainbow you can see on the picture  is just a beautiful effect caused by the  droplets and the Sun this phenomenon has  many different names such as cave um  hole-punch cloud sky punch and false  tree pole if you see one of these  impressive clouds one day make sure you  take a picture and show it to your  friends they'll think you have amazing  photoshop skills ants forming a bridge  it's hard to believe that ads would be  able to stay in such position without  managing to fall right believe it or not  this picture is 100% real and it was  taken by a photographer called a deep  Ryoga Adi posted a series of photos  showing an army of ants that were  stranded in a tree thinking they could  go further the ants quickly realized  they've reached the end of the branch  and started doing some serious damage  control instead of climbing back down  they were determined in a very  impressive real-life scenario the 0.03  inch long ants work  together and created their own bridge to  make it to the other parts of the tree  what you see on the picture are ants  locking legs and making their very own  and bridge to reach the other side and  if you didn't think this is possible let  us remind you how smart insects like  ants bees and termites actually are they  keep track of the distance and the  direction traveled so they can always  know the best way to come back home  this photo is an example of ants  evaluating the situation and working  together to efficiently fix the problem  do you think they actually made it  across busy ants up close let's take it  one step further and debunk some more  pictures people think or Photoshop when  it comes to ant photography we can  totally see how these pictures could  make people think they are staged but  they are not they're just very very  creative they belong to a talented  Russian photographer who goes by the  name of Andrew Pavlov and Rebbe decided  to take on ant macro phot